  "content": {
    "title": "OU women's basketball vs Michigan State score, recap as Sooners return to Sweet 16",
    "text": "March 22, 2026Updated March 23, 2026, 12:24 a.m. CTThe Oklahoma Sooners are facing the Michigan State Spartans in the second round of the Women's NCAA Tournament.A victory would send the Sooners to the Sweet 16 for the second consecutive season.NORMAN — With 2:46 left and Oklahoma up four, the Sooners needed something from their freshman phenom point guard.Aaliyah Chavez was 1 for 8 from deep but found herself with an open look in the corner.Bang.Chavez’s clutch 3 all but ended things as the No. 4 seed Sooners defeated No. 5 seed Michigan State 77-71 Sunday night inside an ear-shattering Lloyd Noble Center. The Spartans shot 43% from the field compared to OU’s 42%.With the win, The Sooners advance to their second straight Sweet 16 and will face either South Carolina or USC in Sacramento. The No. 1 seed Gamecocks and No. 9 seed Trojans play Monday night.Chavez finished with 18 points and six assists. Star center Raegan Beers dominated the paint with 18 points and 14 rebounds.OU outscored MSU 20-17 in the fourth quarter. The Sooners didn’t use a single sub during the final period.Now, the Sooners await their opponent in the Sweet 16.Watch OU women's basketball vs Michigan StateMarch Madness scoreboard: Oklahoma vs Michigan State live score updates7:43 left in 3Q: Oklahoma 45, Michigan State 42 | MSU's Jalyn Brown assessed Flagrant 1, momentum shiftsAs OU's freshman point guard Aaliyah Chavez drove to the basket, she caught a hand to the face.After a review, Michigan State's Jalyn Brown was given a Flagrant 1 foul and Chavez knocked down two free throws. Chavez is up to 11 points.The Sooners have started the period on an 8-0 run.HALF: Michigan State 42, Oklahoma 37 | Sooners trail after sloppy halfOklahoma women's basketball played a sloppy first half.The Sooners took ill-advised shots and committed 14 turnovers. OU is shooting 39% from the field compared to Michigan State's 47%.Star center Raegan Beers has been productive when the Sooners have found her. She has 11 points 3 on 4 of 6 shooting with five rebounds.Freshman phenom Aaliyah Chavez finished the first half with nine points on just 3 for 11 shooting and a 1 for 6 mark from 3.Spartans guard Rashunda Jones leads all scorers with 16 points off the bench.End of 1Q: Michigan State 21, Oklahoma 16 | Spartans hot earlyMichigan State came to play.The Spartans are shooting 53% from the field and have drilled 3 of their 4 3-point attempts. OU is 1 for 6 from deep.MSU guard Rashunda Jones has nine points off the bench.What channel is Oklahoma vs Michigan State on today? How to watch, stream OU women's basketball gameTV: ESPNStreaming: ESPN+ (here's how to stream it live)Oklahoma vs Michigan State will be broadcast on ESPN. It will also be streamed on ESPN+.What time does OU play today? Oklahoma vs Michigan State timeDate: Sunday, March 22Start time: 7 p.m. CTWhere: Lloyd Noble Center in NormanThe Oklahoma vs Michigan State game starts at 7 p.m. Sunday from Lloyd Noble Center in Norman.Oklahoma women's basketball schedule 2025-26All times are Central Standard Time (CST)Monday, Nov. 3: OU 84, Belmont 67Monday, Nov. 10: UCLA 73, OU 59Wednesday, Nov. 12: OU 89, Kansas City 61Friday, Nov. 14: OU 89, North Alabama 61Sunday, Nov. 16: OU 95, Western Carolina 32Wednesday, Nov. 19: OU 112, East Texas A&M 59Friday, Nov. 28: OU 100, Coppin State 46Sunday, Nov. 30: OU 109, Florida State 91Wednesday, Dec. 3: OU 103, NC State 98Sunday, Dec. 7: OU 90, Maryland Eastern Shore 37Thursday, Dec. 11: OU 103, Little Rock 48Saturday, Dec. 13: OU 92, OSU 70Monday, Dec. 22: OU 126, NC Central 54Thursday, Jan 1: OU 72, Texas A&M 50Sunday, Jan 4: OU 95, Mississippi State 47Thursday, Jan 8: Ole Miss 74, OU 69Sunday, Jan 11: Kentucky 63, OU 57Sunday, Jan 18: LSU 91, OU 72Thursday, Jan 22: OU 94, South Carolina 82 (OT)Sunday, Jan 25: OU 72, Auburn 65Thursday, Jan 29: OU 85, Texas A&M 58Sunday, Feb 1: Texas 78, OU 70Monday, Feb 9: Vanderbilt 102, OU 86Thursday, Feb 12: OU 81, Florida 74Sunday, Feb 15: OU 79, Alabama 71Thursday, Feb 19: OU 71, Georgia 67Sunday, Feb 22: OU 100, Tennessee 93Thursday, Feb 26: OU 89, Arkansas 44Sunday, Mar 1: OU 84, Missouri 78Thursday, Mar 5: SEC Tournament: OU 82, Florida 64Friday, Mar 6: SEC Tournament: LSU 112, OU 78Friday, Mar 20: Women's NCAA Tournament: OU 89, Idaho 59Oklahoma vs Michigan State women's basketball highlightsIf X/Twitter feed doesn't load, click HERE.Colton Sulley covers the Oklahoma Sooners for The Oklahoman. Have a story idea for Colton? He can be reached at csulley@oklahoman.com or on X/Twitter at @colton_sulley. Support Colton's work and that of other Oklahoman journalists by purchasing a digital subscription today at subscribe.oklahoman.com.",
